remstart
    THE RAINBOW FISH
    another hidden thing, and a prototype. the routines are in fish_routines_rainbow, and the tests are in
    fish_tests_rainbow.

    A RAINBOW FISH is a fish like any other of its kind, and matches with them, but the line around it is the
    rainbow, and its edge shimmers in it (A RAINBOW FISH in FishEffect.fx: the effect takes 2000 more for one).
    the colors come from where the fish is on the screen, and the time, in waves that go across the board, so
    rainbow fish next to each other look joined (THE WAVES OF A RAINBOW FISH). what it is goes along with it, the way that the way that it faces
    does: a swap trades it, and a fall takes it down (swapCellStacks and copyCellStack, in fish_funcs, call
    rainbowTradeFish and rainbowCopyFish). a rainbow fish that pops scores RAINBOW_FISH_BONUS more, as if its
    place in its group were worth that much more. a fish that comes in to fill the board is never one.

    WHERE THEY COME FROM. a group of RAINBOW_BURST_SIZE fish or more, that matched, and pops, leaves a
    rainbow fish behind, where the cursor is: the fish in that cell does not pop with the group, and as the
    group pops, it swells up and turns into a rainbow fish (rainbowCursorPunch). if the cursor is on a
    rainbow fish that bursts, or on a fish of some other group that pops, the fish that comes in to fill
    the cell is the rainbow fish, once the board has filled back in. there are none when a game starts.
    AND THEY BREED. a group of fish that matched, and pops, beside a rainbow fish, with none in it, brings
    rainbow fish: the fish that come in to fill its cells are rainbow fish. a group with a rainbow fish in it
    uses it up, and brings ordinary fish.
    so that it can be seen to, a band of rainbow light goes across the screen, along the wave, through the
    groups that bring them, one after another (rainbowBreedPlan, before handle_combos pops anything). all
    of each fish that it goes over turns to the rainbow (THE RAINBOW FLOOD in FishEffect.fx). once it has
    gone all the way over a group, it stops there, and the group pops, one fish after another, the way that
    any group does, and RAINBOW_BREED_PAUSE later, the band goes on to the next group along the wave. the
    other groups of the look pop the way that they always do.

    THE BURST. a group of RAINBOW_BURST_SIZE or more, that matched, also sets off every rainbow fish that
    there is. each one counts as one more fish of any group that it touches, so a pair of fish beside it,
    of any kind, which would not pop on their own, makes three with it, and is taken along. they go into
    one forced group (FORCE_RAINBOW), which scores the way that one group of all of them would. a rainbow
    fish that is in a group that pops anyway stays in it, and still takes along what it touches.
    the burst goes before everything else of that look. first a surge goes out from the cursor: a ring
    that bends the water, with a ragged edge (THE SURGE in ScreenEffect.fx), RAINBOW_SURGE_SPEED# pixels a
    millisecond. as it gets to each rainbow fish, the fish is flooded with the rainbow (THE RAINBOW FLOOD in
    FishEffect.fx: the effect takes 1000 more for a fish that is flooded), a rainbow cloud claps out of it,
    and it pops, wherever its group is. what it takes along pops just after it. nothing falls yet: every
    other pop of the look, the big group's too, waits until the surge has got to the last of them, and
    RAINBOW_BURST_AFTER more. then the big group pops, and the fish that the cursor is on swells up into
    the new rainbow fish, with a cloud of its own. then the board fills in. nothing bursts at night.

    THE RAINBOW CLOUDS. a cloud of rainbow light that claps out of a fish into the water behind the board.
    it is not drawn on its own: ScreenEffect.fx turns the ripples of light that the water already has to
    the colors of the rainbow, and makes them brighter, where its ring is, on the water and not the fish
    (THE RAINBOW CLOUDS in ScreenEffect.fx). there are 8 of them, and none of it is worked out while none
    is going.

    THE SAVED GAME. which cells have a rainbow fish is saved with the rest of the game, 30 cells to a number,
    from RAINBOW_PREF on (rainbowSave and rainbowLoad, which fish_routines_save calls). a game that was
    saved before there was any of this has none.

    NONE ARE BROUGHT IN A BURST. from the look that a big group pops on until the board settles, no group
    brings rainbow fish (RAINBOW_NO_BREED), so that once it is over, the only rainbow fish on the board is
    the new one where the cursor was.

    IN A SCHOOL. a rainbow fish that swims off to a school out in the background is a rainbow fish out there
    too (FLOCK_RAINBOW): its edge shimmers in the rainbow (FlockEffect.fx). a burst pops it too, when the
    surge gets to it, with a cloud, the way that the tide's flush pops one (schoolFlushPop). one that swims
    back onto the board is an ordinary fish again. it is saved with the school.

    STILL TO DO. a rainbow fish from a bottle. a whole board of them, which may be an ending. the board
    growing, and a shift that wraps a fish around, do not carry what is rainbow yet. a fish that a quest or
    the diver puts in a cell keeps what the fish before it was.
remend

` THE SAVED GAME. 1 at RAINBOW_PREF when the saved game has these, and then 14 numbers of 30 cells each
global RAINBOW_PREF = 5100

` IN A SCHOOL. 1 for a fish out in the background that left the board as a rainbow fish, and when it pops
` in a burst, on the clock of the game, or 0. how many of them are due to pop.
global dim FLOCK_RAINBOW(48)
global dim RAINBOW_FLOCK_POP_AT(48)
global RAINBOW_FLOCK_DUE = 0
global RAINBOW_FLOCK_LATEST = 1500 `the latest that one pops after the surge set off, however far off it is, in milliseconds
` 1 from the look that a big group pops on until the board settles: no group brings rainbow fish then, so
` that after a burst, the only rainbow fish is the new one where the cursor was
global RAINBOW_NO_BREED = 0

` THE RAINBOW FISH. 1 for each cell that has one. it goes with the fish.
global RAINBOW_FISH_ON = 1 `0 turns them off, for the debug window and the tests
global dim RAINBOW_FISH(400)
global RAINBOW_FISH_BONUS = 5 `how much more a rainbow fish scores when it pops, the way that the 10 of each fish in a group is
global RAINBOW_FISH_COUNT = 0 `how many there are, for the debug window
global RAINBOW_FISH_SPAWN = -1 `the cell that gets a new rainbow fish once the board has filled back in, or -1

` AND THEY BREED. how many of the fish that come in to fill each column, from the top, are rainbow fish, for
` this look at the board, how long a group that brings them lights up for, in milliseconds, which fish are lit
` up, and until when
global dim RAINBOW_FISH_OWED(40)
global RAINBOW_BREED_SPEED# = .0012 `how far along the wave the band goes in a millisecond, between the groups
global RAINBOW_BREED_PAUSE = 250 `how long it waits at a group, after the group's last fish has popped, in milliseconds
` THE WAVE OF A LOOK. for each group, how many milliseconds from when handle_combos laid them out its first
` fish pops, or -1 for a group that brings none. and where the band is along the wave, at times on the
` clock of the game, from one to the next of which it goes in a straight line.
global dim RAINBOW_BREED_WAIT(400)
global dim RAINBOW_BREED_T(100)
global dim RAINBOW_BREED_AT#(100)
global RAINBOW_BREED_STEPS = 0
` what rainbowBreedPlan works out for each group: if there is a rainbow fish in it, how many rainbow fish
` are beside it, how many fish it has, and where its far end is along the wave
global dim RAINBOW_PLAN_HAS(400)
global dim RAINBOW_PLAN_BESIDE(400)
global dim RAINBOW_PLAN_N(400)
global dim RAINBOW_PLAN_FAR#(400)
global dim RAINBOW_PLAN_NEAR#(400)
global RAINBOW_BREED_GAP# = 3 `how many times faster the band crosses the water between two groups
global dim RAINBOW_PLAN_DONE(400)
global dim RAINBOW_BREED_CELLS(400)
global RAINBOW_BREED_FROM = 0
global RAINBOW_BREED_UNTIL = 0
global RAINBOW_BREED_COUNT = 0 `how many groups have brought them, for the tests
` how far along the wave of the rainbow a pixel of the screen is, across and down. FishEffect.fx has these
` too, as RAINBOW_WAVE, and the two have to be kept the same by hand. the band goes from the near end of
` the groups that bring rainbow fish to the far end, and it is RAINBOW_BREED_WIDE# wide.
global RAINBOW_BREED_WAVE_X# = .006
global RAINBOW_BREED_WAVE_Y# = .0035
global RAINBOW_BREED_WIDE# = .15
global RAINBOW_FISH_SEEN = 0 `what rainbowFishBeside found

` THE BURST. how big a group sets it off, the forced group that it pops as, how long after the rainbow fish
` light up the fish that they take along do, and how long the pops wait in all, in milliseconds
global RAINBOW_BURST_SIZE = 5
global FORCE_RAINBOW = 4
global RAINBOW_BURST_GROUP = -1 `the forced group of the burst, on this look at the board, or -1
global RAINBOW_BURST_LIVE = 0 `1 when there is a burst on this look, with any rainbow fish in it
global RAINBOW_BURST_AFTER = 250 `how long after the surge gets to the last rainbow fish the big group pops, in milliseconds
global RAINBOW_BURST_WAIT = 0 `the wait of handle_combos when the surge set off
global RAINBOW_BURST_ALONG = 90 `how long after a rainbow fish what it takes along pops, in milliseconds
` THE SURGE. how fast it goes, in pixels a millisecond, where it set off from, in pixels, when, and how
` long after it got to the last rainbow fish it fades out, in milliseconds
global RAINBOW_SURGE_SPEED# = .3
global RAINBOW_SURGE_X# = 0
global RAINBOW_SURGE_Y# = 0
global RAINBOW_SURGE_AT = 0
global RAINBOW_SURGE_FADE = 500
global RAINBOW_BURST_LAST = 0 `how long the surge takes to get to the last fish of the burst, in milliseconds
` the fish that the cursor is on, which turns into a rainbow fish as the big group pops, or -1, and when
global RAINBOW_CURSOR_KEEP = -1
global RAINBOW_CURSOR_AT = 0
global RAINBOW_CURSOR_PUNCH# = 1.8 `how big it swells as it turns, where 1 is its own size
global RAINBOW_BURST_COUNT = 0 `how many bursts there have been, for the tests
` for each cell, while a burst is going: 1 for a rainbow fish, 2 for a fish that it takes along, or 0
global dim RAINBOW_BURST_CELLS(400)
` and when each of them lights up, on the clock of the game, and when it is over
global dim RAINBOW_BURST_FROM(400)
global RAINBOW_BURST_UNTIL = 0
` and how long after the surge set off each of them pops, in milliseconds, and the rainbow fish that took
` each fish along
global dim RAINBOW_BURST_DELAY(400)
global dim RAINBOW_BURST_BY(400)

` THE RAINBOW CLOUDS. the effect and the sprite, and for each of the 8: where it claps out from, in pixels,
` when, on the clock of the game, and how big it gets, where 1 is about two cells. how long one lasts, in
` milliseconds, how strong they are, from 0 to 1, and how big the one at the cursor is.
global dim RAINBOW_CLOUD_X#(8)
global dim RAINBOW_CLOUD_Y#(8)
global dim RAINBOW_CLOUD_AT(8)
global dim RAINBOW_CLOUD_SIZE#(8)
global RAINBOW_CLOUD_NEXT = 0
global RAINBOW_CLOUD_LIFE = 1800
global RAINBOW_CLOUD_STRENGTH# = .85
global RAINBOW_CLOUD_CURSOR# = 1.6
global RAINBOW_CLOUD_UNTIL = 0 `when the last of them is over

` HOW A RAINBOW FISH LOOKS. see A RAINBOW FISH and THE WAVES OF A RAINBOW FISH in FishEffect.fx, and the
` debug window. its colors come from where it is on the screen, and the time, in waves that go across the
` board, so that rainbow fish near each other look joined. how strongly the edge outside of its line
` shimmers, from 0 to 1, how many waves go by in a second, how much of its line is the rainbow in place of
` its dark color, from 0 to 1, and how pale the colors are, from 0 to 1.
global RAINBOW_RIM# = .9
global RAINBOW_RIM_SPEED# = .35
global RAINBOW_RIM_LINE# = 1
global RAINBOW_RIM_PALE# = .25
` and the waves: the way that they go, as an angle in radians (0 is to the right, and they go down the
` screen as it grows), how long one is in pixels, how many steps the colors come in (0 for colors that
` blend), and how much they bend and ripple (0 for straight)
global RAINBOW_WAVE_ANGLE# = .5
global RAINBOW_WAVE_LONG# = 160
global RAINBOW_WAVE_STEPS# = 0
global RAINBOW_WAVE_SWIRL# = .3

